{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Friend-code entry golden cases run by Android FriendCodeGoldenTest and iOS FriendCodeGoldenTests. normalized is what the add-friend-by-code input becomes before it is sent to the social_send_friend_request RPC (null means the client rejects it as an invalid code and sends nothing). The server accepts only the canonical forms g_ plus 12 lowercase hex digits or p_ plus 32 lowercase hex digits; both clients also accept the display form GYM-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX in any case, ignore case and surrounding whitespace (Unicode spaces, newlines, U+0085, U+200B), and reject anything over 64 UTF-8 bytes, inner spaces or dashes, look-alike letters and full-width characters. display lists how a canonical code is shown to its owner.",
